it were. At the nanotech meeting itself I passed out printed copies
and fully admitted to having authored the piece. ("BlackNet" was the
name I used with the late Phil Salin, founder of AMIX, in 1987-91, to
make the point about black markets in information and how the really
profitable version of AMIX will someday be a kind of BlackNet.)

